        {
          "id": "c6_s01",
          "slideIndex": 0,
          "title": "Subhashita 1 — Desire & Contentment",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s1.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s1.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "अन्तो नास्ति पिपासायास्तुष्टिस्तु परमं सुखम् ।\nतस्मात् सन्तोषमेवेह परं पश्यन्ति पण्डिताः ॥",
          "iast": "anto nāsti pipāsāyāstuṣṭistu paramaṁ sukham |\ntasmāt santoṣameveha paraṁ paśyanti paṇḍitāḥ ||",
          "translation": "There is no end to thirst and desire; contentment is the supreme happiness. Therefore the wise look upon inner contentment as the greatest treasure on earth."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s02",
          "slideIndex": 0,
          "title": "Subhashita 2 — The Mirage of Worldly Possessions",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s2.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s2.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "यत् पृथिव्यां व्रीहि यवं हिरण्यं पशवः स्त्रियः ।\nनालमेकस्य तत् सर्वमिति मत्वा शमं व्रजेत् ॥",
          "iast": "yat pṛthivyāṁ vrīhi yavaṁ hiraṇyaṁ paśavaḥ striyaḥ |\nnālamekasya tat sarvamiti matvā śamaṁ vrajet ||",
          "translation": "If all the grain, gold, cattle, and pleasures of the earth were possessed by a single man, they would still not suffice to satisfy his craving; knowing this, seek serene peace."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s03",
          "slideIndex": 1,
          "title": "Subhashita 3 — The Wise Mourn Neither Living nor Dead",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s3.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s3.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "गतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न शोचति विचक्षणः ॥",
          "iast": "gatāsūnagatāsūṁśca nānuśocanti paṇḍitāḥ |\nsarvathā vartamāno'pi na śocati vicakṣaṇaḥ ||",
          "translation": "The truly wise mourn neither for those whose breath has departed nor for those whose breath remains; knowing the immortal Self, the enlightened man is freed from grief."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s04",
          "slideIndex": 1,
          "title": "Subhashita 4 — The Incurable Disease of Envy",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s4.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s4.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "य ईर्ष्युः परवित्तेषु रूपे वीर्ये कुलान्वये ।\nसुखसौभाग्यसत्कारे तस्य व्याधिरनन्तकः ॥",
          "iast": "ya īrṣyuḥ paravitteṣu rūpe vīrye kulānvaye |\nsukhasaubhāgyasatkāre tasya vyādhiranantakaḥ ||",
          "translation": "He who is envious of another's wealth, beauty, valour, high birth, happiness, good fortune, and honour suffers from an incurable, endless disease."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s05",
          "slideIndex": 2,
          "title": "Subhashita 5 — Knowledge vs. Fleeting Ease",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s5.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s5.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "सुखार्थी वा त्यजेद् विद्यां विद्यार्थी वा त्यजेत् सुखम् ।\nसुखार्थिनः कुतो विद्या कुतो विद्यार्थिनः सुखम् ॥",
          "iast": "sukhārthī vā tyajed vidyāṁ vidyārthī vā tyajet sukham |\nsukhārthinaḥ kuto vidyā kuto vidyārthinaḥ sukham ||",
          "translation": "The seeker of ease must give up knowledge; the seeker of knowledge must give up ease. For whence can the ease-seeker find knowledge, and whence can the student find ease?"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s06",
          "slideIndex": 2,
          "title": "Subhashita 6 — The Greatest Wonder of the World",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s6.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s6.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "अहन्यहनि भूतानि गच्छन्तीह यमालयम् ।\nशेषाः स्थावरमिच्छन्ति किमाश्चर्यमतः परम् ॥",
          "iast": "ahanyahani bhūtāni gacchantīha yamālayam |\nśeṣāḥ sthāvaramicchanti kimāścaryamataḥ param ||",
          "translation": "Yudhiṣṭhira to the Yakṣa: 'Day after day creatures depart for the abode of Death; yet those who remain believe they will live forever. What can be more astounding than this?'"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s07",
          "slideIndex": 3,
          "title": "Subhashita 7 — The Four Tests of Gold & Man",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s7.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s7.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "यथा चतुर्भिः कनकं परीक्ष्यते निघर्षणच्छेदनतापताडनैः ।\nतथा चतुर्भिः पुरुषः परीक्ष्यते त्यागेन शीलेन गुणेन कर्मणा ॥",
          "iast": "yathā caturbhiḥ kanakaṁ parīkṣyate nigharṣaṇacchedanatāpatāḍanaiḥ |\ntathā caturbhiḥ puruṣaḥ parīkṣyate tyāgena śīlena guṇena karmaṇā ||",
          "translation": "As gold is tested in four ways—by rubbing, cutting, heating, and hammering—so a human being is tested in four ways: by sacrifice, character, virtues, and righteous actions."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s08",
          "slideIndex": 3,
          "title": "Subhashita 8 — Universal Family (Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam)",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s8.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s8.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "अयं निजः परो वेति गणना लघुचेतसाम् ।\nउदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुम्बकम् ॥",
          "iast": "ayaṁ nijaḥ paro veti gaṇanā laghucetasām |\nudāracaritānāṁ tu vasudhaiva kuṭumbakam ||",
          "translation": "'This person is mine, that one is a stranger'—such is the reckoning of the narrow-minded. But for those of noble heart, the entire world is one beloved family."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s09",
          "slideIndex": 3,
          "title": "Subhashita 9 — Knowledge: The Indestructible Wealth",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s9.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s9.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "न चौरहार्यं न च राजहार्यं न भ्रातृभाज्यं न च भारकारि ।\nव्यये कृते वर्धत एव नित्यं विद्याधनं सर्वधनप्रधानम् ॥",
          "iast": "na caurahāryaṁ na ca rājahāryaṁ na bhrātṛbhājyaṁ na ca bhārakāri |\nvyaye kṛte vardhata eva nityaṁ vidyādhanaṁ sarvadhanapradhānam ||",
          "translation": "It cannot be stolen by thieves, confiscated by kings, divided by brothers, nor is it burdensome to carry. The more it is spent, the more it increases; the wealth of learning is supreme!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s10",
          "slideIndex": 4,
          "title": "Subhashita 10 — The Deception of Fleeting Desires — Bhartrihari",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s10.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s10.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "भोगा न भुक्ता वयमेव भुक्तास्तपो न तप्तं वयमेव तप्ताः ।\nकालो न यातो वयमेव यातास्तृष्णा न जीर्णा वयमेव जीर्णाः ॥",
          "iast": "bhogā na bhuktā vayameva bhuktāstapo na taptaṁ vayameva taptāḥ |\nkālo na yāto vayameva yātāstṛṣṇā na jīrṇā vayameva jīrṇāḥ ||",
          "translation": "Bhartṛhari's Nītiśatakam: 'Pleasures were not consumed by us, we ourselves were consumed; austerities were not endured, we were consumed; time did not pass away, we passed away; cravings have not grown old, we alone have grown old!'"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s11",
          "slideIndex": 4,
          "title": "Subhashita 11 — Pure Speech Alone Is the Immortal Ornament",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s11.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s11.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "केयूरा न विभूषयन्ति पुरुषं हारा न चन्द्रोज्ज्वला\nन स्नानं न विलेपनं न कुसुमं नालङ्कृता मूर्धजाः ।\nवाण्येका समलङ्करोति पुरुषं या संस्कृता धार्यते\nक्षीयन्ते खलु भूषणानि सततं वाग्भूषणं भूषणम् ॥",
          "iast": "keyūrā na vibhūṣayanti puruṣaṁ hārā na candrojjvalā\nna snānaṁ na vilepanaṁ na kusumaṁ nālaṅkṛtā mūrdhajāḥ |\nvāṇyekā samalaṅkaroti puruṣaṁ yā saṁskṛtā dhāryate\nkṣīyante khalu bhūṣaṇāni satataṁ vāgbhūṣaṇaṁ bhūṣaṇam ||",
          "translation": "Neither bracelets, nor moon-bright necklaces, nor perfumes, nor adorned locks adorn a person. Culture-refined speech (Saṁskṛtā Vāṇī) alone is true ornament; all jewels decay, the ornament of speech is eternal!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s12",
          "slideIndex": 4,
          "title": "Subhashita 12 — The Four Classes of Men in the World",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s12.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s12.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "एते सत्पुरुषाः परार्थघटकाः स्वार्थां परित्यज्य ये\nसामान्यास्तु परार्थमुद्यमभृतः स्वार्थाविरोधेन ये ।\nतेऽमी मानुषराक्षसाः परहितं स्वार्थाय निघ्नन्ति ये\nये निघ्नन्ति निरर्थकं परहितं ते के न जानीमहे ॥",
          "iast": "ete satpuruṣāḥ parārthaghaṭakāḥ svārthāṁ parityajya ye\nsāmānyāstu parārthamudyamabhṛtaḥ svārthāvirodhena ye |\nte'mī mānuṣarākṣasāḥ parahitaṁ svārthāya nighnanti ye\nye nighnanti nirarthakaṁ parahitaṁ te ke na jānīmahe ||",
          "translation": "Noble men sacrifice their own good for others; ordinary men help others when not conflicting with their own interest; demonic men destroy others' good for their own gain; but those who destroy others' good for no reason at all—we know not who they are!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s13",
          "slideIndex": 5,
          "title": "Subhashita 13 — The Obstinate Fool — Bhartrihari",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s13.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s13.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "लभेत सिकतासु तैलमपि यत्नतः पीडयन्\nपिबेच्च मृगतृष्णिकासु सलिलं पिपासादितः ।\nकदाचिदपि पर्यटञ्छशविषाणमासादयेत्\nन तु प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खजनचित्तमाराधयेत् ॥",
          "iast": "labheta sikatāsu tailamapi yatnataḥ pīḍayan\npibecca mṛgatṛṣṇikāsu salilaṁ pipāsāditaḥ |\nkadācidapi paryaṭañchaśaviṣāṇamāsādayet\nna tu pratiniviṣṭamūrkhajanacittamārādhayet ||",
          "translation": "One might extract oil by squeezing sand, quench thirst from a desert mirage, or find a horn upon a hare; but never can one reason with the heart of an obstinate fool!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s14",
          "slideIndex": 5,
          "title": "Subhashita 14 — Caraiveti: The March Forward (Aitareya Brahmana 1)",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s14.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s14.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "नानाश्रान्ताय श्रीरस्तीति रोहित शुश्रुम ।\nपापो नृषद्वरो जन इन्द्र इच्चरतः सखा ।\nचरैवेति चरैवेति ॥",
          "iast": "nānāśrāntāya śrīrastīti rohita śuśruma |\npāpo nṛṣadvaro jana indra iccarataḥ sakhā |\ncaraiveti caraiveti ||",
          "translation": "From the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa: 'There is no fortune for him who does not strive, O Rohita! The sedentary man stagnates; Indra is the steadfast companion of the traveller. March on! March on!'"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s15",
          "slideIndex": 5,
          "title": "Subhashita 15 — Caraiveti: The Blossoming Soul (Aitareya Brahmana 2)",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s15.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s15.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "पुष्पिण्यौ चरतो जङ्घे भूष्णुरात्मा फलग्रहिः ।\nशर्शेस्य सर्वे पाप्मानः श्रमेण प्रपथे हताः ।\nचरैवेति चरैवेति ॥",
          "iast": "puṣpiṇyau carato jaṅghe bhūṣṇurātmā phalagrahiḥ |\nśarśesya sarve pāpmānaḥ śrameṇa prapathe hatāḥ |\ncaraiveti caraiveti ||",
          "translation": "The legs of the wanderer blossom; his spirit grows and bears fruit. All his weaknesses are slain by purposeful toil along the path. March on! March on!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s16",
          "slideIndex": 6,
          "title": "Subhashita 16 — Caraiveti: The Four Ages in Action (Aitareya Brahmana 3)",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s16.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s16.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "कलिः शयानो भवति सञ्जिहानस्तु द्वापरः ।\nउत्तिष्ठंस्त्रेता भवति कृतं सम्पद्यते चरन् ।\nचरैवेति चरैवेति ॥",
          "iast": "kaliḥ śayāno bhavati sañjihānastu dvāparaḥ |\nuttiṣṭhaṁstretā bhavati kṛtaṁ sampadyate caran |\ncaraiveti caraiveti ||",
          "translation": "Lying asleep, man is Kali; waking up, he is Dvāpara; standing upright, he is Tretā; moving forward in action, he creates the Golden Age (Satya Yuga)! March on! March on!"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s17",
          "slideIndex": 6,
          "title": "Subhashita 17 — The One Divine Truth Expressed Variously",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s17.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s17.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "एकं सद् विप्रा बहुधा वदन्त्यग्निं यमं मातरिश्वानमाहुः ।\nसत्यमेकं परं ब्रह्म सर्वभूतेषु संस्थितम् ॥",
          "iast": "ekaṁ sad viprā bahudhā vadantyagniṁ yamaṁ mātariśvānamāhuḥ |\nsatyamekaṁ paraṁ brahma sarvabhūteṣu saṁsthitam ||",
          "translation": "Ṛgveda 1.164.46: The Truth is One; the wise speak of it in varied ways, calling it Agni, Yama, Mātariśvan—the Supreme Brahman seated in the hearts of all beings."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s18",
          "slideIndex": 7,
          "title": "Subhashita 18 — Righteous Wealth (Dharmenaiva Samaharet)",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s18.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s18.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ।\nधर्मेणैव समाहर्तव्यं वित्तं धर्मेण योजयेत् ॥",
          "iast": "yato dharmastato jayaḥ |\ndharmeṇaiva samāhartavyaṁ vittaṁ dharmeṇa yojayet ||",
          "translation": "Where there is righteousness, there is victory. Wealth should be earned through righteous means and dedicated to noble service."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s19",
          "slideIndex": 7,
          "title": "Subhashita 19 — The Mind As Master — Dhammapada in Sanskrit",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s19.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s19.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "मनःपूर्वङ्गमा धर्मा मनोश्रेष्ठा मनोमयाः ।\nमनसा चेत् प्रसन्नोन भाषते वा करोति वा ।\nततस्तं सुखमन्वेति छाया वाऽनपायिनी ॥",
          "iast": "manaḥpūrvaṅgamā dharmā manośreṣṭhā manomayāḥ |\nmanasā cet prasannona bhāṣate vā karoti vā |\ntatastaṁ sukhamanveti chāyā vā'napāyinī ||",
          "translation": "From the Dhammapada: 'Mind precedes all phenomena; mind is their chief; they are made of mind. If one speaks or acts with a serene mind, happiness follows him like a never-departing shadow.'"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s20",
          "slideIndex": 7,
          "title": "Subhashita 20 — Hatred Ceases by Love Alone — Dhammapada",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s20.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s20.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "न हि वैरेण वैराणि शाम्यन्तीह कदाचन ।\nअवैरेणैव शाम्यन्ति एष धर्मः सनातनः ॥",
          "iast": "na hi vaireṇa vairāṇi śāmyantīha kadācana |\navaireṇaiva śāmyanti eṣa dharmaḥ sanātanaḥ ||",
          "translation": "Never in this world does hatred cease through hatred; it ceases only through love and non-hatred. This is the eternal law (Dharma Sanātana)."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s21",
          "slideIndex": 8,
          "title": "Subhashita 21 — The Fragrance of Good Deeds — Dhammapada",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s21.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s21.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "न पुष्पगन्धः प्रतिवातमेति न चन्दनं तगरं मल्लिका वा ।\nसतां तु गन्धः प्रतिवातमेति सर्वा दिशः सत्पुरुषः प्रवाति ॥",
          "iast": "na puṣpagandhaḥ prativātameti na candanaṁ tagaraṁ mallikā vā |\nsatāṁ tu gandhaḥ prativātameti sarvā diśaḥ satpuruṣaḥ pravāti ||",
          "translation": "The fragrance of flowers does not travel against the wind, neither sandalwood nor jasmine; but the fragrance of the righteous travels even against the wind, filling all quarters."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6_s22",
          "slideIndex": 8,
          "title": "Subhashita 22 — The True Sage (Śāntakāyo Śāntavāk) — Dhammapada",
          "m4a": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s22.m4a",
          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap6/chapter6s22.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "न मुण्डनेन श्रमणो ह्यव्रतोऽनृतं भणन् ।\nशान्तकायो शान्तवाक् शान्तमनाः सुसमाहितः ।\nवान्तलोकामिषो भिक्षुरुपशान्त इति चोच्यते ॥",
          "iast": "na muṇḍanena śramaṇo hyavrato'nṛtaṁ bhaṇan |\nśāntakāyo śāntavāk śāntamanāḥ susamāhitaḥ |\nvāntalokāmiṣo bhikṣurupaśānta iti cocyate ||",
          "translation": "Not by a shaved head is one a true monk if devoid of vows and speaking untruth. He whose body is serene, whose speech is peaceful, whose mind is tranquil and concentrated, who has renounced worldly desire—he is called truly peaceful."
        }
