          "iast": "śreyaśca preyaśca manuṣyametastau samparītya vivinakti dhīraḥ |\nśreyo hi dhīro'bhi preyaso vṛṇīte preyo mando yogakṣemād vṛṇīte ||",
          "translation": "Kaṭha Upaniṣad 1.2.2: 'The Good (Śreya) and the Pleasant (Preya) approach man. The wise examine both and distinguish between them. The wise choose the Good over the Pleasant; the fool chooses the pleasant for the sake of worldly gain.'"
