          "mp3": "assets/audio/chap7/chapter7s18.mp3",
          "sanskrit": "दूरमेते विपरीते विषूची अविद्या या च विद्येति ज्ञाता ।\nविद्याभीप्सिनं नचिकेतसं मन्ये न त्वा कामा बहवोऽलोलुपन्त ॥",
          "iast": "dūramete viparīte viṣūcī avidyā yā ca vidyeti jñātā |\nvidyābhīpsinaṁ naciketasaṁ manye na tvā kāmā bahavo'lolupanta ||",
          "translation": "Kaṭha Upaniṣad 1.2.4: 'Far apart and leading to opposite goals are these two: Ignorance (Avidyā) and Wisdom (Vidyā). I know you, Naciketas, as an earnest seeker of Knowledge, whom countless worldly pleasures could not distract.'"
