          "iast": "śravaṇāyāpi bahubhiryo na labhyaḥ śṛṇvanto'pi bahavo yaṁ na vidyuḥ |\nāścaryo vaktā kuśalo'sya labdhā''ścaryo jñātā kuśalānuśiṣṭaḥ ||",
          "translation": "Kaṭha Upaniṣad 1.2.7: 'He whom many cannot even hear of, whom many hearing do not comprehend: wonderful is the teacher who expounds Him, skilled is he who attains Him, and wonderful is the seeker who knows Him when taught by an adept!'"
